<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states the PDE, the steady state, the periodic boundary, the 60 µm scale and the 0 Ma age. math_kg_loops yaml points each law at a function range and a Lean theorem. Six Lean theorems, zero sorry, cover monotonicity of the wavelength count, age-independence, the 10/480/600 µm counts, and the trace-gap sign at ratio 1 and ratio 12. Deduction: the Lean trace gap uses integer stand-ins (fu = 4, |gv| = 5) rather than the real Jacobian entries 0.8 and -1 (-8). The yaml loci were written against this commit's line numbers." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "jacobian() (L85-L104) is the Schnakenberg steady state u* = a + b, v* = b/(a+b)² with trace -0.2 and det 1. dispersion_sigma (L107-L114) is the larger eigenvalue of J - k²D, and simulate_schnakenberg (L160-L200) is a periodic Fourier IMEX step with implicit diffusion. The Holocene ratio Dv/Du = 12 opens the Turing gap; Du = Dv closes it (self-test). Deduction: Du and Dv are spatial calibrations to the assigned 60 µm scale, not values from Schnakenberg (1979) or from a sand-dollar experiment (-6). Schnakenberg's paper is about limit cycles; the spatial extension is the standard one but it is an extension (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py L70–L76: Du and Dv are frozen calibrations to the 60 µm slot, not measured diffusivities <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/2340b0d2/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L70-L76>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Equilibrated FFT wavelength 60.336 µm against the 60 µm slot (not copied: the value is the spectrum, the reference is the assignment). Pearson r of linear versus FFT wavelengths is 0.9965, RMSE 2.575 µm. Specimen foreground fraction 0.357 against a single-test prior of 0.70, union circularity 0.066 against 1, coherency 0.404 against a noise prior of 0.25. Nearest-neighbour spacing mean is 42.84 µm, which is not forced equal to 60 µm. Deduction: the KS statistic 0.143 is exactly 1/7, the resolution of a 7-point two-sample test, so it barely constrains the residual distribution (-8). Per-disc shape is not yet measured (-6)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py L216–L224: KS sample size is the seven sweep points <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/2340b0d2/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L216-L224>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-10-m-predecessor-scale-amplitude>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-peak-versus-equilibrated-wavelength-pearson-r>,
