<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength (Echinarachnius parma)",
        "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength faithfully reproduces Echinarachnius parma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Echinarachnius parma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Echinarachnius parma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A measured echinochrome diffusion constant, a gene-regulatory network for E. parma pigment, or a fit to the centimetre-scale petaloid",
        "does_not_claim: That sibling slot 160's dimensionless parameters (α = 1.71, β = 0.43) apply at 60 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivity-scale sweep with Pearson r = 0.9965, RMSE = 2.575 µm; equal-diffusion ablation amplitude 5.69e-3; 10 µm patch amplitude 0",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Linear dispersion peak λ = 61.343 µm and equilibrated FFT wavelength λ = 60.336 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Fourier IMEX integration of the Schnakenberg system on a 480 µm patch, Du = 28.006 µm²/time, Dv = 336.069 µm²/time (ratio 12), seed 3214",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Union-mask segmentation of the CC0 USNM E39365 plate (foreground fraction 0.357, union circularity 0.066, coherency 0.404)",
        "reported_in_source: Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) short-range activation with long-range inhibition; Kondo and Miura (2010) review of reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v, published for limit cycles and used here as the standard two-species Turing extension",
        "reported_in_source: Seilacher (1979) constructional morphology of the sand-dollar test at centimetre scale (petaloids, dome, pressure drainage)",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) diffusion-driven instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator",
        "transfer_boundary: Du and Dv are chosen so the equilibrated lattice sits on the assigned 60 µm detail scale. They are not measured diffusion coefficients of sand-dollar epithelium.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 60 µm wavelength is the slot scale. Seilacher (1979) does not report it.",
        "transfer_boundary: The chronoseries has one member (Holocene, 0 Ma). The predecessor and successor contrasted here are scale tiers (10 µm and 600 µm), not older named species.",
        "transfer_boundary: The rendered disc is a 480 µm patch coloured with the plate's mean pigment. It is not a photograph of a whole test, and the union mask does not separate the three individuals." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Echinarachnius parma" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Echinarachnius" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Echinarachnius parma; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) diffusion-driven instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v, published for limit cycles and used here as the standard two-species Turing extension | Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) short-range activation with long-range inhibition; Kondo and Miura (2010) review of reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework | Seilacher (1979) constructional morphology of the sand-dollar test at centimetre scale (petaloids, dome, pressure drainage); reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Fourier IMEX integration of the Schnakenberg system on a 480 µm patch, Du = 28.006 µm²/time, Dv = 336.069 µm²/time (ratio 12), seed 3214 | Linear dispersion peak λ = 61.343 µm and equilibrated FFT wavelength λ = 60.336 µm | Diffusivity-scale sweep with Pearson r = 0.9965, RMSE = 2.575 µm; equal-diffusion ablation amplitude 5.69e-3; 10 µm patch amplitude 0 | Union-mask segmentation of the CC0 USNM E39365 plate (foreground fraction 0.357, union circularity 0.066, coherency 0.404); transfer_boundary: Du and Dv are chosen so the equilibrated lattice sits on the assigned 60 µm detail scale. They are not measured diffusion coefficients of sand-dollar epithelium. | The 60 µm wavelength is the slot scale. Seilacher (1979) does not report it. | The chronoseries has one member (Holocene, 0 Ma). The predecessor and successor contrasted here are scale tiers (10 µm and 600 µm), not older named species. | The rendered disc is a 480 µm patch coloured with the plate's mean pigment. It is not a photograph of a whole test, and the union mask does not separate the three individuals.; does_not_claim: A measured echinochrome diffusion constant, a gene-regulatory network for E. parma pigment, or a fit to the centimetre-scale petaloid | That sibling slot 160's dimensionless parameters (α = 1.71, β = 0.43) apply at 60 µm]; phenomenon_size: 68 µm (6.84e-05 m, log10=-4.165 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 68 µm to 10.7 cm): 68 µm:echinarachnius-parma-bioelectric-polarity, 240 µm:echinarachnius-parma-vertex-packing, 2.4 mm:echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength, 4.3 mm:echinarachnius-parma-clock-wavefront, 1.4 cm:echinarachnius-parma-morphogen-condensation, 1.9 cm:echinarachnius-parma-flux-canalization, 2.0 cm:echinarachnius-parma-elastic-buckling, 2.4 cm:echinarachnius-parma-branching-tree" ;
